  "children": [
    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "Vrb0t",
      "x": 200,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Direction Contract",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 400,
      "content": "THESIS: This page proves bounded autonomy with the artifact — a policy-gated Terraform change landing in the customer's own Git — instead of asserting an operating model. It refuses the enterprise-AI hero of a claim floated over an abstract isometric diagram.\n\nOWN-WORLD: Linear, pinned by brief. One near-black ground (#08090A / #0E0F11), hairline structure (#1F2023), two-tone text, StackGen purple #9437FF as the only accent. Inter medium for display, JetBrains Mono for code, policy output and measurement only. No gradients, no glow shadows, no eyebrows.\n\nSTORY: An on-call SRE sees the mechanism run, finds the refusal line that earns CAB sign-off, recognises the agent that maps to their job, and books a demo.\n\nFIRST VIEWPORT: Headline left at 56px above a full-width change surface — intent, generated Terraform diff, Tirith policy verdict, merge target — with the customer logo row sitting on the hero's base rule. Primary action in the nav and inline beneath the headline.\n\nFORM: Brief-pinned world (Linear); the direction roll is superseded by the pin per new-work, so there is no seed key.\n\nFINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance"
    },
